### Scaling Real-Time Across Multiple Servers

When you have multiple WebSocket servers, a message sent to server A won't reach users connected to server B. **Pub/Sub** solves this.

```
User A (on server 1)  sends message to room "general"
User B (on server 2)  should receive it
User C (on server 2)  should receive it

Without Pub/Sub: User B and C never get the message.

With Pub/Sub (Redis):
Server 1 publishes to Redis channel "room:general"
Server 2 is subscribed to "room:general" → delivers to B and C
```

#### Socket.IO Redis Adapter

```js
import { createAdapter } from '@socket.io/redis-adapter';
import { createClient } from 'redis';

const pubClient = createClient({ url: process.env.REDIS_URL });
const subClient = pubClient.duplicate();

await Promise.all([pubClient.connect(), subClient.connect()]);

io.adapter(createAdapter(pubClient, subClient));

// Now io.to('room').emit() works across all servers automatically
```

